# INVWINRL.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: the row count on
# lists longer than the window, the seed's three items and the sixty of
# TEST/KEYS/RLLONG.REQ at Box B2, so the count is the list's own and not
# the rows shown.  A backup taken; the item list then counts one more
# after an add and a copy saved, one less after a delete, none after a
# copy left by ESC, one more after a split, the count kept over a
# maximized and restored frame.  Search results for Long count one less
# after a delete, Box B2's contents one less after an item moved out to
# Office, and the item list, opened again, holds what is left; the
# restore of the backup counts the list again, as it was backed up.  From
# a row on the list's third page Record > Parts shows that item's parts,
# none, and ESC opens the list again on that row.  The end by Exit.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINRL.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER
S OPEN
K ALT-A B
T .
K ENTER
S BACKEDUP
K ENTER HOME
S BKCOUNT
# a new item, its note, then the count
K INS
T SYS
K ALT-M
T Compaq
K ALT-L
T A1
K ENTER
S ADDED
K HOME
S ADDCOUNT
# item 5 deleted
K HOME DOWN DOWN DOWN DOWN DEL Y
S DELETED
K HOME
S DELCOUNT
# item 1's copy saved: 5 TABs from the category reach the quantity
K HOME CTRL-D TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB
T 2
K ENTER
S COPIED
K HOME
S CPYCOUNT
# a copy left unchanged by ESC is deleted again
K HOME CTRL-D
S COPY
K ESC
S COPYESC
K PGDN
S CEPGDN
# one of item 2's two units split off
K HOME DOWN ALT-C U
T 1
K ENTER
S SPLIT
K HOME
S SPLCOUNT
K ALT-SPACE X
S MAX
K ALT-SPACE R
S RESTORE
# search results: the third deleted
K ALT-S T
T Long
K ENTER
S FOUND
K HOME DOWN DOWN DEL Y
S FDEL
K HOME
S FDELCNT
K ESC ESC
S BACKITEM
# Box B2's contents: the first row moved out to Office
K ALT-L B DOWN DOWN ENTER
S CONT
K HOME ALT-C M
T OFF
K ENTER
S MOVED
K HOME
S MOVCNT
K ESC
S TREE
K ESC
S ITEMS
# the backup restored: the list counted again
K ALT-A R
T .
K ENTER Y
S RESTORED
K ENTER HOME
S RSTCOUNT
# the row left, two pages down, kept by ESC on its parts
K PGDN PGDN DOWN DOWN ALT-C P
S LPARTS
K ESC
S LBACK
K ALT-F X
